WEBVTT

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:05.384
Next-token prediction scales because text comes from a discrete, fixed vocabulary.

00:00:05.384 --> 00:00:06.282
Audio doesn't.

00:00:06.662 --> 00:00:10.231
So turn the waveform into tokens, train on the tokens, and turn

00:00:10.231 --> 00:00:11.420
them back into sound.

00:00:14.585 --> 00:00:15.708
Hi, I'm Fintan!

00:00:15.708 --> 00:00:17.579
A language model predicts integers.

00:00:17.579 --> 00:00:20.573
Speech is twenty-four thousand real numbers a second.

00:00:20.573 --> 00:00:22.445
A codec sits in between.

00:00:23.825 --> 00:00:25.775
Every neural codec has three parts.

00:00:25.775 --> 00:00:29.024
An encoder squeezes time into a few vectors a second.

00:00:29.404 --> 00:00:32.038
A quantiser turns each vector into integers.

00:00:32.038 --> 00:00:34.671
A decoder turns integers back into sound.

00:00:35.950 --> 00:00:38.247
The old way is residual quantisation.

00:00:38.247 --> 00:00:40.545
Codebook one picks the nearest vector.

00:00:40.925 --> 00:00:44.716
Codebook two quantises what is left over, and so on, each correction

00:00:44.716 --> 00:00:45.979
smaller than the last.

00:00:47.617 --> 00:00:49.468
Here is a toy in two dimensions.

00:00:49.468 --> 00:00:52.641
Each code is a correction to the codes before it, and the

00:00:52.641 --> 00:00:54.228
path closes in on the point.

00:00:54.648 --> 00:00:57.411
Now let the model get code one slightly wrong.

00:00:57.411 --> 00:01:01.402
The later codes still describe the old leftover, so the whole path misses.

00:01:01.822 --> 00:01:04.190
Grouped scalar quantisation throws the codebooks away.

00:01:04.190 --> 00:01:08.248
Each of four numbers is rounded to its own grid of levels.

00:01:08.668 --> 00:01:10.171
Twelve groups make twelve tokens.

00:01:10.171 --> 00:01:13.780
A wrong code for one group moves one number by one step.

00:01:13.780 --> 00:01:15.283
The others are still right.

00:01:16.658 --> 00:01:17.713
Liquid's own figure.

00:01:17.713 --> 00:01:20.876
Four numbers, with eight, seven, six and six levels.

00:01:21.256 --> 00:01:24.511
Together they pick one of two thousand and sixteen codes.

00:01:24.511 --> 00:01:26.464
Twelve groups, twelve tokens a frame.

00:01:28.067 --> 00:01:29.912
The bill is three numbers multiplied.

00:01:30.332 --> 00:01:31.924
Twelve and a half frames a second.

00:01:33.573 --> 00:01:36.929
Twelve codes a frame, so a hundred and fifty tokens a second.

00:01:37.349 --> 00:01:38.587
About eleven bits each.

00:01:38.587 --> 00:01:41.993
Mimi with twelve codebooks lands on the same bitrate, which makes

00:01:41.993 --> 00:01:43.231
it a fair rival.

00:01:45.242 --> 00:01:49.867
Inside, the encoder starts from a spectrum, seventy-five a second, stacks six

00:01:49.867 --> 00:01:52.950
into one, and runs an eight-block LFM3 stack.

00:01:53.330 --> 00:01:57.423
The decoder runs the same stack, then predicts a spectrum and lets

00:01:57.423 --> 00:01:59.469
an inverse FFT make the samples.

00:01:59.469 --> 00:02:01.174
No learned upsampling at all.

00:02:02.517 --> 00:02:06.260
On Liquid's eight test sets it has the best perceptual quality score

00:02:06.260 --> 00:02:08.755
and the lowest mel distance on every one.

00:02:09.175 --> 00:02:11.462
The PESQ score goes the other way.

00:02:11.462 --> 00:02:13.096
NanoCodec wins seven of eight.

00:02:13.516 --> 00:02:16.715
And in text to speech, its tokens give the lowest error rate

00:02:16.715 --> 00:02:18.048
on four sets of eight.

00:02:19.383 --> 00:02:23.346
That is the better experiment: the same backbone, data and compute,

00:02:23.346 --> 00:02:24.787
only the codec changed.

00:02:24.787 --> 00:02:26.588
Mimi doubles the error rate.

00:02:28.725 --> 00:02:32.254
A speech codec's real customer is the language model that has

00:02:32.254 --> 00:02:33.538
to predict its tokens.

00:02:35.900 --> 00:02:39.141
Round instead of chain, keep the bitrate, decode the spectrum.

00:02:39.141 --> 00:02:40.114
Thanks for watching!

00:02:40.534 --> 00:02:42.635
Every source is in the full article.

00:02:42.635 --> 00:02:43.235
I'm Fintan.

00:02:43.235 --> 00:02:43.535
Bye!
